use, modification or redistribution), duration, and any conditions.
An authorization certificate must carry a unique authorization ID, issue date,
and the Licensor's signature, including a verifiable electronic signature.
The Licensor must confirm its issuance through the public GitHub account
identified above or a contact channel verified through that account.
The licensee must retain the signed document and the issuance confirmation.
A request, payment, star, unanswered message, verbal claim, unsigned template
or unverified screenshot is not an authorization. No automatic approval applies.
Private proof need not be posted publicly and should not be committed to Git.
The official copy of this license is sufficient evidence for use permitted by
section 2; individual certificates are needed only for exceptions.

